Subject: Overdispersion: F Test or Chisq Test
Message-ID: <CI0xsdquTPo.3N3oXlYbCgAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/CI0xsdquTPo/m/3N3oXlYbCgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Altuna,

Is there a consensus on whether to use the F-Test or Chisq-Test when correction for overdispersion during calculateDiffMeth? I see from the vignette that F-test is the default when correcting for overdispersion but the Chisq-test can also be specified. I was wondering if F-test should strictly be used since that is the default, and in what cases one could use the Chisq-test.

Thanks for your help,

Brett

From uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com  Thu Nov  2 22:41:01 2017
From: uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com (Altuna Akalin)
Date: Thu, 02 Nov 2017 22:41:01 +0000
Subject: Re: [methylkit_discussion] Overdispersion: F Test or Chisq Test
Message-ID: <CI0xsdquTPo.yoysAbhcCgAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <CI0xsdquTPo.3N3oXlYbCgAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
References: <CI0xsdquTPo.3N3oXlYbCgAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/CI0xsdquTPo/m/yoysAbhcCgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chisq with over-dispersion seems to perform better, if you want to decrease false-positives without curbing too many of the true positives.

Best,
Altuna

